Notebook[{Cell["FermiWick", "Title"], 
  Cell["A guided tour: fermion operators, Wick's theorem, mean field", 
   "Subtitle"], Cell["0. Welcome", "Section"], 
  Cell["FermiWick does by computer the algebra one does on paper with fermion \
ladder operators: products brought to normal order, local operators \
(densities, spins, double occupancy) kept compact and recognized in the \
results, expectation values by Wick's theorem in a Gaussian state that you \
declare, the mean-field Hamiltonian of an operator of any order, Gutzwiller \
projectors, the same operators as matrices for exact diagonalisation, and \
LaTeX of everything.", "Text"], Cell["How to use this notebook: evaluate the \
cells in order (Shift+Enter, or Evaluation > Evaluate Notebook); the whole \
tour takes a few seconds. The comment at the end of each input cell says what \
you should get. The same file runs as a script: math -script Examples.wl. The \
showcase (Showcase/FermiWick_Showcase.pdf) goes through everything in detail, \
and the manual describes every function.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Loading the package", "Subsection"], Cell["(* the paclet next to this \
file (the repository), otherwise the installed one *)\nWith[{folder = \
Quiet[If[$InputFileName =!= \"\", DirectoryName[$InputFileName], \
NotebookDirectory[]]]},\n  If[StringQ[folder],\n   \
Scan[If[FileExistsQ[FileNameJoin[{#, \"PacletInfo.wl\"}]], \
PacletDirectoryLoad[#]] &, {FileNameJoin[{folder, \"FermiWick\"}], \
folder}]]];\nNeeds[\"FermiWick`\"]; Needs[\"FermiWick`Gutzwiller`\"]; \
Needs[\"FermiWick`Fock`\"];", "Input"], 
  Cell["$FermiWickVersion\n(* the version of the package, e.g. \"0.3.0\" *)", 
   "Input"], Cell["1. Writing operators", "Section"], 
  Cell["c[i, s] annihilates a fermion on site i with spin s, cDag[i, s] \
creates it; the spin is SpinUp, SpinDown or a symbol, and sites can be \
symbols. ** multiplies in the given order; NormalOrder moves every cDag to \
the left.", "Text"], Cell["NormalOrder[c[1, SpinUp] ** cDag[1, SpinUp]]\n(* 1 \
- cDag[1, up] ** c[1, up]: the anticommutation relation *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["NormalOrder[c[i, SpinUp] ** cDag[j, SpinUp]]\n(* -cDag[j, up] ** c[i, \
up]: different symbolic sites are different sites *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["hopping = Sum[cDag[1, s] ** c[2, s], {s, $Spins}];\nPlusHC[t \
hopping]\n(* the hopping between sites 1 and 2 plus its Hermitian conjugate, \
four terms *)", "Input"], Cell["2. Local operators and spins", "Section"], 
  Cell["Densities, spins, double occupancy (DOp), doublons (B, Bdag) and \
projectors stay compact; ToSpinChargeBasis writes any expression with them \
and recognizes the spin operators on several sites.", "Text"], 
  Cell["ToSpinChargeBasis[SpOp[1] \\[CenterDot] SmOp[1]]\n(* n/2 + Sz - D on \
site 1: the algebra of one site *)", "Input"], Cell["ToSpinChargeBasis[SdotS[\
1, 1]]\n(* 3/4 n - 3/2 D: a spin 1/2 only on singly occupied sites *)", 
   "Input"], Cell["ToSpinChargeBasis[OperatorCommutator[SdotS[1, 2], SdotS[2, \
3]]]\n(* -I S1.(S2 x S3): the scalar chirality *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["3. Gaussian states and Wick's theorem", "Section"], 
  Cell["A Gaussian state is fixed by its contractions; declare it by its \
symmetries, and ContractionTable shows what survives. WickVEV gives \
expectation values.", "Text"], Cell["state = GaussianState[{\"SpinRotation\", \
\"Charge\"}, \"Filling\" -> 1/2];\nMatrixForm[ContractionTable[state, {1, 2}, \
\"Normal\"]]\n(* hopping chi_12 between the sites, 1/2 on each site, nothing \
between opposite spins *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["WickVEV[SdotS[1, 2], state]\n(* -3/2 |chi_12|^2 *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["pairing = GaussianState[\"SpinRotation\", \"Filling\" -> 1/2, \
\"OnSitePairing\" -> 0];\nWickVEV[SdotS[1, 2], pairing]\n(* -3/2 (|chi_12|^2 \
+ |Delta_12|^2): hopping and singlet pairing enter with the same weight *)", 
   "Input"], Cell["4. Any labels, and states by rules", "Section"], 
  Cell["A state can be declared by rules for its contractions, with any spin \
structure: here a hopping that flips the spin.", "Text"], 
  Cell["flip = GaussianState[{{cDag[i_, s_], c[j_, t_]} :> If[i === j, \
KroneckerDelta[s, t]/2, If[s === t, g, h]]}];\nWickVEV[SzOp[1] ** SzOp[2], \
flip]\n(* (h^2 - g^2)/2: the spin-flip hopping h enters with the opposite \
sign *)", "Input"], Cell["Modes can carry any labels: DeclareModeLabels says \
what each label is. With orbitals, the anticommutator gives a delta of the \
orbitals:", "Text"], Cell["DeclareModeLabels[{\"Site\", \"Orbital\", \
\"Spin\"}];\nNormalOrder[c[1, a, SpinUp] ** cDag[1, b, SpinUp]]\n(* \
KroneckerDelta[a, b] - cDag[1, b, up] ** c[1, a, up] *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["5. Mean field", "Section"], Cell["MeanField gives the \
Hartree-Fock-Bogoliubov Hamiltonian of an operator of any order: two \
operators kept out in every way, the rest contracted. The fields are its \
coefficients.", "Text"], Cell["MeanField[U DOp[1], \
GaussianState[\"SpinRotation\", \"Filling\" -> \\[Nu], \"OnSitePairing\" -> \
\\[Eta]]]\n(* Hartree terms U nu n and BCS terms with eta, plus the constant \
*)", "Input"], Cell["fields = OperatorCoefficients[MeanField[-Jc \
SdotScrossS[i, j, k], pairing]];\nfields[cDag[i, SpinUp] ** c[j, SpinUp]]\n(* \
the hopping field of the bond i -> j: (3 I/4) Jc (chi_jk chi_ki + Delta*_jk \
Delta_ki), with chi_ki = Conjugate[chi_ik] *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["6. Gutzwiller projectors", "Section"], 
  Cell["real = GaussianState[{\"SpinRotation\", \"Charge\", \
\"TimeReversal\"}, \"Filling\" -> 1/2];\nhop2 = Sum[cDag[1, s] ** c[2, s] + \
cDag[2, s] ** c[1, s], {s, \
$Spins}];\nSimplify[GutzwillerVEV[LocalSandwich[GutzwillerProjector, {1, 2}, \
hop2], real]/WickVEV[hop2, real]]\n(* Sin[2 theta]^2: the Gutzwiller \
reduction of the hopping, 8 d (1 - 2 d) with d = Sin[theta]^2/2 *)", 
   "Input"], Cell["7. Matrices and exact diagonalisation", "Section"], 
  Cell["FermiWick`Fock` writes any operator as a sparse matrix on the Fock \
space of a few sites, or on a sector with fixed N and Sz: the modes are the \
ladder operators, numbered site by site with the spin fastest.", "Text"], 
  Cell["sector = FockSector[FockSpace[{1, 2}], \"N\" -> 2, \"Sz\" -> \
0];\nEigenvalues[Normal[FockMatrix[-t hop2 + U (DOp[1] + DOp[2]), \
sector]]]\n(* the Hubbard dimer: 0, U and (U -+ Sqrt[U^2 + 16 t^2])/2 *)", 
   "Input"], Cell["{e, v} = LowestStates[FockMatrix[-hop2 + 4 (DOp[1] + \
DOp[2]), sector], 1];\nFockExpectation[SdotS[1, 2], First[v], sector]\n(* \
about -0.64: the two spins of the ground state form mostly a singlet *)", 
   "Input"], Cell["8. LaTeX", "Section"], Cell["ToTeX[ToSpinChargeBasis[Opera\
torCommutator[SdotS[1, 2], SdotS[2, 3]]]]\n(* \"-i \\mathbf \
S_{1}\\cdot(\\mathbf S_{2}\\times\\mathbf S_{3})\" *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["WickTeX[cDag[1, SpinUp] ** c[2, SpinUp] ** cDag[2, SpinUp] ** c[1, \
SpinUp], state]\n(* Wick's theorem written out, with the contractions drawn \
(LaTeX package simpler-wick) *)", "Input"]}, Visible -> True, 
 WindowTitle -> "FermiWick \[Dash] guided tour", 
 StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
